{"parentUuid":"c1563124-e799-40b8-9140-5d64549edb3e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a43b3a0aed36748db","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyY9VEbD861YG8Qk9N6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4514,"cache_read_input_tokens":92187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CezyY8af6etTQg7UPKjLi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1708161-d8c4-4ffb-8df7-4b8fa339a21a","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:36:30.088Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f1708161-d8c4-4ffb-8df7-4b8fa339a21a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a43b3a0aed36748db","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyY9VEbD861YG8Qk9N6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no repeated user corrections in the last 7 days. The one pair that looked like a repeat was not a correction. I found four rules that are now false, two rules that clash with other instructions, and three identity facts to check. I changed no files.\n\n## 1. Rules findings\n\n### (a) Rules contradicted by what happened\n\n1. **`~/DEV/CLAUDE.md` says \"23 projects carry their own CLAUDE.md\".** I measured 132 git repos with a CLAUDE.md at depth 2 or less, not counting `_ARCHIVE`. Session `3945b73d` (2026-09-09) added a CLAUDE.md to every repo during the GitHub move (\"68 repos pushed, each with AGENTS.md… a CLAUDE.md\"). The \"last checked 2026-09-05\" date is older than that move.\n   *Proposed:* \"Most project repos carry their own CLAUDE.md (~130 as of 2026-09-13).\"\n2. **`~/DEV/CLAUDE.md` says \"~155 skills\".** `~/.claude/skills` now has 66 folders and 42 `SKILL.md` files at depth 2. Session `7741462f` (2026-09-12) said \"Your skills got cut from ~160 to 63\". Memory `project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md` says the same.\n   *Proposed:* \"~65 skills (after the 2026-09-12 audit).\"\n3. **Memory `project_backup-sync-system.md` says \"Windows retired 2026-08-14\".** It says this in 3 places. But `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and USER.md both say the Windows laptop is still active. The 2026-09-12 session also found a real Windows backup problem (\"Your Windows laptop has **no working backup**\"). Only the Windows scheduled tasks were retired on 08-14, not the machine.\n   *Proposed:* \"The Windows scheduled tasks were retired 2026-08-14. The machine itself is still active.\"\n4. **USER.md says \"Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md\".** `machine.md` says the path list has one home, `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`. The pointer in USER.md is out of date.\n5. **The `status-report` skill clashes with the ELI5 rule of \"2 options max\".** In session `497f3a39` (2026-09-07 to 09-09), 4 assistant turns asked 2 to 5 numbered questions at once. The user replied \"1. Cut track 2. no idea here 3. not mine 4. …\". The skill tells the agent to do this: `SKILL.md:225` says \"targeted gap questions, then the four standing ones\". So the agent followed the skill, and the skill breaks the style rule.\n   *Proposed:* \"Interview skills may ask up to 2 questions per turn under ELI5.\"\n6. **The dcg memory misses one blocked shape (small).** In session `c59d1788` (2026-09-12), dcg blocked `cat > \"$DIR/file\" <<'EOF'`. `project_dcg-guard-blocks.md` only lists `rm -rf` inside heredocs and `git` inside `$(…)`.\n   *Proposed:* add \"writing a file with a heredoc (`cat > … <<EOF`) also blocks\".\n\nRules the agent kept (checked, no break found):\n- It used no `timeout` command.\n- It ran no global `pip install`. The hits I found were text inside documents, not commands.\n- It did not read DexaProject data. Its only DexaProject commands were repo checks with `gh`.\n- It surfaced `.errors.log` today: session `9823c1f0` opened with the compiler-lock note. The log still holds one entry, `compiler-stale-lock … 1550min` (2026-09-13 04:30).\n- The router is up to date: `PlayCalls` is listed in `FOOTBALL.md`.\n- The SessionStart hook did not fail. All 31 \"could not read\" matches were quotes of the rule text inside memory docs.\n\nNote on `.errors.log`: it is tracked in the synced `claude-global-memory` repo. In session `40af6584` (2026-09-11) it caused a merge conflict and a rejected push. No rule covers this. *Proposed:* \"`.errors.log` is per-machine. Do not commit it, or git-ignore it.\"\n\n### (b) Corrections the user gave twice or more\n\n**None found.** The candidate pair was \"trim it\" (`75960c5c`, 2026-09-05, and `9422b1a6`, 2026-09-09). Both times it meant \"trim MEMORY.md\". The agent had just offered that (\"Option A… I merge finished threads and cut dead lines\"). It was not a complaint about answer length.\n\nSome confusion showed up only once each, so none of it counts as repeated:\n- `7741462f` (09-12): \"what windows file? what do I need to run?\"\n- `9c319715` (09-08): \"show me the full email draft\". The agent had given a file path, not the text.\n- `f1097c6d` (09-12): \"no I understand how this would work…\"\n\nIf more of these appear, the ELI5 rule \"what do I do now\" could say: \"When I ask to see something, paste it. Don't give only the path.\"\n\n## 2. Identity findings (USER.md)\n\n1. **Kids' ages may be stale.** USER.md says Rowan is \"10mo as of 2026-09-01\". The June-era sources say \"Rowan (10 months)\" too. That includes the Windows KeystoneOS memory file `user_personal_constitution.md` and ContextVault `context.md`. The Career doc is dated Jun 8, and its copies only got a new timestamp on Sep 9. Both cannot be right: either Rowan's age or the \"as of\" date is out of date. Ask Eric.\n2. **\"No cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval\" is broader than what he actually does.** I found:\n   - 8 `com.keystone.*` launchd jobs loaded on this Mac;\n   - all projects on private GitHub;\n   - data backed up to Google Drive.\n   The rule probably means \"no Baylor data or systems on outside services without approval\". Ask Eric and reword it.\n3. **\"OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks\" looks out of date.** Projects now live in `~/DEV` and sync through GitHub. OneDrive shows up only for Baylor documents, such as the inventory xlsx in `9c319715`.\n\nConfirmed, no conflict:\n- Title and employer: Director of Applied Performance, Baylor.\n- Wife Kristina; the three kids' names.\n- Career goal near Iowa: the only source is the Jun 8 Career doc, and I found no newer evidence against it.\n- Python + R: 919 R files and 694 .py files changed in the last 90 days.\n- macOS is primary and Windows is still active.\n- The `~/DEV/ContextVault` path exists.\n\n## 3. Checked\n\n- **Transcripts:** 94 `.jsonl` files changed in the last 7 days (85 main sessions, 9 subagent files). About 25 human sessions had messages dated 2026-09-05 to 09-13. That leaves out the memory-compiler and morning-briefing automation. Some of these are the same session resumed: `3945b73d`/`7755f8f2`, `a2d1f472`/`b8143861`, `555f113f`/`80892ff4`.\n- **Date filter:** I filtered by message date from 09-06, except the 09-05 \"trim it\" context. The mtime search also picked up synced Windows sessions dated 08-03 to 08-14. I skipped those for rules.\n- **Method:** Python pulled out user text (147 user turns after an assistant turn), tool-use commands, tool results (dcg blocks, rejections), and the assistant turn before each correction. I also counted options and questions per assistant turn.\n- **Live checks:** `which -a`, launchd list, skill, CLI and CLAUDE.md counts, `.errors.log`, hook source, `settings.json` (`outputStyle: ELI5` is active).\n- **memsearch queries (11):**\n  - kids ages\n  - career target Iowa\n  - Director title\n  - Windows retired or active\n  - Baylor IT and schedulers (twice, reworded)\n  - ContextVault career context\n  - job search\n  - Iowa relocation\n  - wife, kids, school\n  - R usage\n\n## 4. Not checked\n\n- **Identity, 90 days:** I did not review 90 days of transcripts. I only covered the 7-day sessions above plus memsearch results, which come mostly from memory files, ContextVault docs and June compiled logs. I did not read Windows-machine transcripts from June to August for identity facts. I did not read ContextVault docs in full.\n- **Subagent transcripts:** not read.\n- **Codex sessions:** not checked (outside `~/.claude/projects`).\n- **Artifact rule:** \"never conclude 'it already exists'\" needs a judgment on each request. I only did a light check.\n- **Session routine:** `git pull` + `STATUS.md` lives in each repo's AGENTS.md, not in the rule sources. Not checked.\n- **Quote:** `3945b73d` (\"68 repos pushed…\") is past the one-short-quote limit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4514,"cache_read_input_tokens":92187,"output_tokens":3458,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":382},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4514},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":3458,"cache_read_input_tokens":92187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezyY8af6etTQg7UPKjLi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9d3a979-539b-43ff-95ea-03e925b1ceaa","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:36:59.432Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
